  abstract = {The activity coefficients of KCl in aqueous KCl--Me4NCl have been determined from emf measurements using a potassium ion-selective electrode and an Ag/AgCl electrode at four values of the total ionic strengths, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0 and 3.0 mol kg--1 at 25, 35 and 45 {$^\circ$}C. The values of log {$\gamma$}KCl were found to vary linearly with the ionic strength fraction of the second electrolyte, in accordance with the `Harned rule'. This indicates that the thermodynamic properties of these mixtures are determined primarily by binary interactions of the type K--Me4N. The results are discussed in light of the Pitzer, Scatchard and Reilly--Wood--Robinson treatments.},
